# M3-T4c: apps/mobile's start/android/ios scripts set EXPO_NO_TYPESCRIPT_SETUP=1
# inline (VAR=value cmd), the normal POSIX way to scope an env var to one
# command. Neither PowerShell nor cmd.exe understands that syntax, so without
# this setting the same package.json script fails differently on Andy's
# Windows machine than it does in CI's bash. shell-emulator=true makes pnpm
# run package.json scripts through its own bundled JS shell (a bash-like
# parser, not the OS shell), so the exact same script text works identically
# on Windows and in CI. This is a pnpm feature, not a new dependency (CLAUDE.md
# rule 11 does not apply): no cross-env package added.
# https://pnpm.io/npmrc#shell-emulator
shell-emulator=true
